# ADR 0006: Auto-suggestion uses Tier 2 double-progression

**Date:** 2026-08-02
**Status:** Accepted

## Context
The app should suggest next-session weights based on prior 
performance, but the mechanism must be transparent, cheap to 
build, and toggleable.

## Decision
Use double-progression logic:
- If last session hit the top of the rep range on all working sets: 
  suggest +increment (per-exercise setting, e.g. +2.5 kg compound, 
  +1.25 kg isolation).
- If last session hit at least the bottom of the range on all sets: 
  suggest same weight, +1 rep target.
- If last session missed the bottom: suggest same weight, repeat.

Toggleable globally in Settings and per-exercise. Suggested values 
appear pre-filled but always editable.

Progression lookup is scoped to the current program 
(programExercise-based). Ad-hoc exercises (programExercise == nil) 
look up the Exercise's most recent LoggedExercise across all history.

## Alternatives considered
- **Tier 1 (show last session only, no suggestion):** Too passive.
- **Tier 3 (RIR-based):** Requires per-set RIR logging discipline; 
  can be added later.
- **Tier 4 (e1RM stagnation detection):** Complements Tier 2 but is 
  display/analytics, not a suggestion engine.

## Consequences
- Simple rule, easy to explain, matches natural progression logic.
- Per-exercise increment field required on Exercise model.
- e1RM display can be added later as an analytics view without 
  affecting suggestion logic.

